{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr4zl6nk8f5","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"jepa prediction component planned alongside executable world model","summary":"User's team is adding a JEPA (joint embedding predictive architecture) prediction component to the ARC-AGI-3 stack alongside the executable-world-model harness. Integration seams to keep open in the EWM design: (1) JEPA as a learned latent dynamics predictor could serve games the symbolic step() cannot model (the modelability-poor fallback path), (2) as a divergence prior at EXECUTE time (predicted-frame checks could compare against JEPA embedding distance instead of exact cells), (3) as a candidate ranker during SYNTHESIZE (prefer programs whose rollouts agree with JEPA predictions), (4) the recorded TransitionSuite corpora (out/ewm-runs/*/transition-suite.json, growing per run) are exactly JEPA training data — keep persisting them. Prior art in-competition: the 0.79 public-score notebook used a LeWM/JEPA dynamics model (Akhil Tolani). Status: user-owned workstream; EWM harness should not block on it but should not close these seams.","category":"preference","tags":["arc-agi-3","jepa","project-direction"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T13:46:12.848Z","vec":[-0.10629168897867203,-0.006463663652539253,-0.022862669080495834,-0.008471252396702766,0.0507051907479763,0.0267191119492054,-0.10992178320884705,0.05044953525066376,-0.0049185059033334255,-0.01648813858628273,0.005446727853268385,-0.05225910618901253,0.011063896119594574,0.017832156270742416,0.06622286885976791,-0.036794137209653854,0.0688965693116188,0.04071139171719551,-0.0800234004855156,-0.07684113830327988,-0.01847798563539982,-0.030342118814587593,0.04431254789233208,-0.03012114018201828,0.023238936439156532,-0.028298411518335342,0.0273533184081316,0.08563818037509918,-0.019694261252880096,-0.04702898859977722,-0.06188485771417618,-0.03140726685523987,-0.026729766279459,-0.02815203182399273,-0.07267860323190689,0.003328